WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.990
The Waimakariri District Council meeting for
December was recently held, and before getting

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:13.900
to down to business, the Councillors and Mayor
David Ayers had the pleasure of presenting

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.260
a Community Service Award to Kaiapoi resident,
John Rose.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:22.040
John was recognized for his volunteer efforts
in the community, including his work with

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.400
North Canterbury Mini Bus Trust.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:31.680
The Council then moved on to deputations and
presentations, and heard from both Andrew

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:37.149
Gough, a resident of Swannanoa and developer,
Bevan Hames, on the proposal to reduce a section

00:00:37.149 --> 00:00:41.760
of Tram Road from 100km to 80km.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:47.160
After considerable debate, council approved
the recommendation that the speed limit be

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:54.980
reduced from 100km/h to 80km/h on Tram Road
from 500m east of the Bradley Road / McHughs

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:59.220
Road intersection to 300m west of that intersection.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:06.440
Council also approved an expansion of options
to the kerbside collection service to be added

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:09.920
into the Waste Management and Minimisation
plan 2017.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:15.620
After a large amount of public consultation,
Option C has been chosen as the preferred

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:20.520
option, which allows users a choice of new
rates-funded bins for rubbish and organics,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:25.140
or sticking with the user-pays rubbish bags
and rates-funded recycling bin they currently use.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.439
The final details of the proposed new kerbside
collection service will be presented to the

00:01:30.439 --> 00:01:36.869
Council in the final draft Waste Minimisation
Plan next year after the 2018-2028 Long Term

00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:38.700
Plan has been approved.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.929
Council also adopted the Northern Pegasus
Bay Bylaw 2016 implementation plan, which

00:01:45.929 --> 00:01:49.390
includes the establishment of the Northern
Pegasus Bay advisory group.

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:52.820
This group will be chaired by Councillor Al
Blackie.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.840
And Council approved the legal stopping and
physical removal of Hood Avenue and Clarke

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.249
Avenue in The Pines Beach area.

00:02:01.249 --> 00:02:06.260
The removal of these now redundant roads is
another step forward in the Regeneration process.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:12.640
This meeting was the last for the year, with
Council’s first ordinary meeting in the

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.500
new year on Tuesday 6th February.

